  "investigation_notes": "Upload failure investigated. Diagnosis: database dependency network failure, not storage.\n\nRoot cause:\n- Database container `incidentlab-db-1` is detached from all Docker networks (E5 `networks: []`), while app `incidentlab-app-1` is on `incidentlab_default` (E4).\n- This breaks service-name DNS: app logs show both upload and health failing with `psycopg.OperationalError: failed to resolve host 'db': [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution` (E3).\n\nSymptoms caused by it:\n- App is `running` (E1) but `/health` returns 503 `{\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n- Health-check code path fails at `psycopg.connect(DATABASE_URL...)` in `health` (E3), same as `upload` path at `main.py:65` (E3).\n\nDependency itself is healthy \u2014 ruled out DB crash:\n- DB `state: running`, `status: Up 10 seconds (healthy)` (E1), `health: healthy`, `exit_code: 0`, `oom_killed: false` (E5).\n- DB logs: `database system is ready to accept connections`, listening on `5432` (E6).\n- Recent `health_status: healthy` and `exec_die exit 0` for `pg_isready` (E7).\n\nStorage ruled out as cause for uploads stopping:\n- Bind mount present: `source: /srv/lab-data` -> `destination: /data`, `rw: true` (E4).\n- Filesystem `/srv/lab-data`: `use_percent: 9.0`, `available_mb: 410.6`, `inode_use_percent: 0.2` (E8) \u2014 not full.\n- Upload dir `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is dir, `owner 1000:1000`, `mode 0755` (E9), app runs as `1000:1000` (E4), `app_user_can_write: true` (E9) \u2014 writable.\n- No OOM/error in app inspect: `oom_killed: false`, `error: null`, `exit_code: 0` (E4).\n\nContext:\n- Both containers were re-created/restarted at `00:00:24` and `00:01:10` (`create/kill/stop/die/destroy/rename/start` for both) (E7), with current `started_at` `00:01:10` for DB (E5) and `00:01:16` for app (E4). `restart_count: 0` for both (E4,E5) indicates recreate, not in-container restart loop.\n\nConclusion: Uploads fail because app cannot resolve/connect to `db` due to DB network detachment. Repair requires re-attaching `incidentlab-db-1` to `incidentlab_default` (person approval required, no change made).\n",
